WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.112 --> 00:00:16.296
The sun rose as it did every other day, promising light and warmth, but today, no amount of

2
00:00:16.356 --> 00:00:19.237
sunshine could brighten the March sisters' darkened hearts.

3
00:00:20.057 --> 00:00:24.999
While Meg and Jo, who had not slept a wink all night, watched for any signs of change

4
00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:28.520
in Beth's condition, they talked about what to do with Amy.

5
00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:32.642
"Obviously she can't stay here," stated Meg.

6
00:00:32.662 --> 00:00:34.084
"Maybe Mr.

7
00:00:34.124 --> 00:00:36.946
Laurence and Laurie can look after her," suggested Jo.

8
00:00:36.966 --> 00:00:40.489
"That wouldn't be proper," Meg said, shaking her head.

9
00:00:40.509 --> 00:00:45.533
"Besides, they've done so much for us already we couldn't burden them with anything more."

10
00:00:46.454 --> 00:00:51.959
At the same moment the sisters thought of their only other solution, but both of them were hesitant

11
00:00:51.979 --> 00:00:59.864
to say it until finally Meg said, "We are left with no other choice but "Yes, Aunt March's,"

12
00:01:00.305 --> 00:01:04.126
sighed Jo, finishing Meg's words and already feeling sorry for Amy.

13
00:01:04.146 --> 00:01:08.807
"If you can talk with Aunt March, then I'll break the news to Amy," said Meg.

14
00:01:09.927 --> 00:01:12.448
As the girls were agreeing to the plan, Dr.

15
00:01:12.488 --> 00:01:17.489
Bangs, looking as though he hadn't had much sleep as well, returned to check up on Beth.

16
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:23.091
Again, the kind doctor told Meg and Jo that he was concerned about them, and that they must

17
00:01:23.191 --> 00:01:26.952
look after themselves first in order to be better caregivers to Beth.

18
00:01:27.948 --> 00:01:28.629
Leaving Dr.

19
00:01:28.669 --> 00:01:32.472
Bangs to tend to Beth, Meg and Jo closed the door firmly behind them.

20
00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:38.317
"We'd better go and talk to Amy," said Meg, holding out her hand for the key to the

21
00:01:38.337 --> 00:01:44.502
bedroom. Although it was cruel to lock Amy up, it was the only way they could keep her

22
00:01:44.562 --> 00:01:45.303
away from Beth.

23
00:01:46.204 --> 00:01:50.827
Having unlocked the door, Meg and Jo expected Amy to come flying at them in a fit.

24
00:01:52.008 --> 00:01:58.145
However, they found her eerily quiet as she sat on the floor, hugging her knees close, her eyes

25
00:01:58.285 --> 00:01:59.365
swollen from crying.

26
00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.346
"Is Beth dead?"

27
00:02:01.846 --> 00:02:03.127
was Amy's first question.

28
00:02:03.927 --> 00:02:09.610
Although she did not know the details, Amy was extremely shrewd and could sense the seriousness of Beth's

29
00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:10.910
illness without being told.

30
00:02:12.311 --> 00:02:16.412
Meg squatted down beside her and said in a motherly voice, "It's all right.

31
00:02:16.692 --> 00:02:18.033
Everything is going to be fine."

32
00:02:18.053 --> 00:02:20.434
"Dr. Bangs is with her now.

33
00:02:20.854 --> 00:02:26.541
She's stable for the time being, but there hasn't been any improvement in her condition," Jo said truthfully.

34
00:02:26.561 --> 00:02:32.706
"Beth has scarlet fever and that means you mustn't be in the house or else you will catch

35
00:02:32.766 --> 00:02:34.007
it too," said Meg.

36
00:02:34.027 --> 00:02:36.049
"But where will I go?"

37
00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:36.989
asked Amy.

38
00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:41.853
"You need to go and stay with Aunt March," Meg said carefully.

39
00:02:42.874 --> 00:02:48.078
After two seconds of stunned silence, Amy replied: "No!

40
00:02:48.459 --> 00:02:50.400
I won't stay with that old lady.

41
00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.022
She gives me the creeps!"

42
00:02:53.283 --> 00:02:57.865
"Amy!" Meg said sharply, "You must never speak about our relative in that manner.

43
00:02:58.445 --> 00:03:01.046
And you have no say in the matter, I'm sorry to say.

44
00:03:01.606 --> 00:03:04.727
Pack a few things, please, and get ready to leave immediately."

45
00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:12.449
Amy argued, begged, cried, and shouted, but in the end, she saw her sisters' decision was firm.

46
00:03:14.409 --> 00:03:19.371
After a wearisome visit with Aunt March where Jo had to endure criticism of her parents and their

47
00:03:19.431 --> 00:03:24.192
upbringing of the girls, Jo's relative finally agreed to allow Amy to stay with her.

48
00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:30.844
Laurie, on the other hand, proved his loyalty as a friend once again by wholeheartedly offering to do

49
00:03:30.884 --> 00:03:32.025
whatever he could to help.

50
00:03:33.065 --> 00:03:36.448
"Laurie, can't I stay with you and your grandfather?"

51
00:03:36.888 --> 00:03:40.250
Amy asked him as the Laurence carriage was taking them to Aunt March's.

52
00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:47.515
"I wish you could, Amy," Laurie answered, "but your sisters have made up their minds and you must

53
00:03:47.695 --> 00:03:48.696
honor their decision."

54
00:03:49.476 --> 00:03:51.277
Amy crossed her arms and pouted.

55
00:03:52.318 --> 00:03:58.546
Smiling at her childish gesture, Laurie said, "But I promise to visit every day as your messenger, and

56
00:03:58.626 --> 00:04:01.869
I'll update you on Beth's condition and other things happening at home."

57
00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:08.493
Amy's eyes brightened and she flashed a big lovely smile, saying, "Oh, would you, Laurie?

58
00:04:08.833 --> 00:04:09.974
That would be grand.

59
00:04:10.354 --> 00:04:11.495
Thank you so much."

60
00:04:12.596 --> 00:04:17.179
The remainder of the journey was filled with light talk and giggling as the two made an extra

61
00:04:17.219 --> 00:04:19.040
effort not to mention Beth's illness.

62
00:04:20.612 --> 00:04:25.135
Amy had been with her family to Aunt March's house several times but had never been there by

63
00:04:25.175 --> 00:04:30.159
herself. She immediately felt intimidated, uncomfortable, and alone.

64
00:04:30.179 --> 00:04:36.003
"Well, at least you're not starving at home, as you seem to have grown since the last time

65
00:04:36.103 --> 00:04:40.226
I saw you," snapped the old woman, scrutinizing Amy from head to toe.

66
00:04:41.246 --> 00:04:47.551
Aunt March was a critical, difficult, and stubborn person who usually got her way because she was very

67
00:04:47.611 --> 00:04:49.192
wealthy and powerful in the community.

68
00:04:50.132 --> 00:04:53.853
However, when it came to her only relative, her nephew Mr.

69
00:04:53.873 --> 00:04:59.215
March, she found that he would not give in to her even though she threatened to withhold any

70
00:04:59.295 --> 00:05:00.795
financial help he might need.

71
00:05:01.675 --> 00:05:04.676
Mr. March always kept his ground and never asked her for money.

72
00:05:05.757 --> 00:05:11.218
Even though Aunt March would never admit it, she respected her nephew's sense of values and had a

73
00:05:11.278 --> 00:05:12.979
soft spot for her grandnieces.

74
00:05:13.799 --> 00:05:20.357
She loved Jo for her honesty and colorful character, which brought life to her otherwise boring existence, and

75
00:05:20.477 --> 00:05:23.198
Amy, for her beauty, good manners, and ambition.

76
00:05:23.218 --> 00:05:28.439
"There are some rules you must obey in this house," Aunt March warned.

77
00:05:28.459 --> 00:05:32.240
"One, you must never shout or raise your voice.

78
00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.341
Two, you must never run around the house.

79
00:05:36.341 --> 00:05:41.123
If you break or damage anything, you will pay for it, even if you have to come work

80
00:05:41.163 --> 00:05:42.683
for me for the rest of your life.

81
00:05:43.483 --> 00:05:46.084
Three, meals are served at set times.

82
00:05:46.644 --> 00:05:48.545
If you are late, then you do not eat.

83
00:05:49.306 --> 00:05:53.948
Four, you will be given chores and expected to complete them by the time given."

84
00:05:53.968 --> 00:05:58.111
"More chores," Amy sighed under her breath.

85
00:05:58.131 --> 00:05:59.812
"What did you say?"

86
00:06:00.232 --> 00:06:02.853
Aunt March's sharp ears picked up Amy's mumbling.

87
00:06:02.873 --> 00:06:08.096
"Nothing, Aunt March," muttered Amy, wishing she could calm her shaky legs.

88
00:06:08.116 --> 00:06:14.420
"Five," continued the old woman, "you will sit and read to me every afternoon.

89
00:06:15.328 --> 00:06:19.510
"Your sister used to do that, but she got lazy, then she got sick.

90
00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.851
I don't know what to do with that girl.

91
00:06:22.651 --> 00:06:27.534
Six Amy sighed inwardly and wished she were at home with the others.

92
00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:32.916
Surely, getting sick was not as bad as having to listen to and obey all of Aunt March's

93
00:06:32.976 --> 00:06:36.458
rules. "How am I going to survive?"

94
00:06:36.938 --> 00:06:38.138
Amy wondered to herself.

95
00:06:40.659 --> 00:06:45.886
Accepting her plight, Amy decided the only way she was going to manage her stay at Aunt March's

96
00:06:46.086 --> 00:06:48.068
was to do exactly as she demanded.

97
00:06:48.088 --> 00:06:54.071
"Don't rub too hard or you might scratch my good silver," Aunt March snapped at Amy, who was

98
00:06:54.131 --> 00:06:55.752
polishing endless silver ornaments.

99
00:06:55.772 --> 00:06:59.194
"Careful!" screeched Aunt March's parrot, Polly.

100
00:06:59.214 --> 00:07:04.397
"Yes, ma'am, I'll be very careful," Amy answered dutifully.

101
00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:11.789
While Amy carried on with her chores, Aunt March watched her secretly and thought, "Yes, this one has

102
00:07:11.889 --> 00:07:15.070
hope. She can be useful in society.

103
00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:17.371
This one is a lady."

104
00:07:17.391 --> 00:07:20.353
"Careful!" Polly screeched again.

105
00:07:21.933 --> 00:07:23.174
Back home, Dr.

106
00:07:23.234 --> 00:07:27.095
Bangs increased the dose of medicine, but Beth's fever still persisted.

107
00:07:28.136 --> 00:07:31.898
Even though Jo felt totally hopeless and useless, she refused to give up.

108
00:07:32.858 --> 00:07:37.340
She continued to do everything she could to take care of Beth in the way she knew best.

109
00:07:37.972 --> 00:07:43.783
And so Jo opened an old book and began reading softly, “A beautiful dream was about to come

110
00:07:43.843 --> 00:07:45.967
true for Princess Anastasia
